# q6_design
Task 6, stage 4  design and calculations

assumptions
  students              : 200000
  lectures              : 4000, mean 800 MB, 90 minutes
  streaming bitrate     : 5 Mbps
  peak concurrent share : 5% of the students
  segment for seeking   : 4 MB

capacity
  catalogue             : 3200 GB = 3.2 TB
  with two copies       : 6.4 TB
  one lecture per minute: 8.89 MB
  segments per minute   : 2.22 of 4 MB

reads to start playback at an arbitrary minute
  contiguous allocation : 1 read (one seek to the segment)
  indexed allocation    : 2 reads (the index block, then the segment)
  linked allocation     : 1024 reads (walk 4 MB of 4 KB blocks)
  the index entry for a 4 MB segment needs 1024 pointers of 4 bytes
  with one index block per 4 MB, the whole 2 GB lecture needs
  512 segments and 512 index blocks: 2048 KB of metadata per lecture

throughput at the peak
  concurrent streams    : 10000
  aggregate bitrate     : 50.0 Gbps
  two 10 Gbps server NICs would carry 20 Gbps, so the peak
  cannot be served from one site: a CDN is required, or the peak
  must be spread over many servers.

transfer per month
  2000000 views x 800 MB = 1600000 GB = 1.60 PB
  at 0.02 USD per GB through a CDN: 32000 USD per month

capacity check for the chosen allocation
  one 4 MB segment as 4 KB blocks = 1024 blocks
  a 4 KB index block holds 1024 pointers, so one index block
  covers 1024 blocks = 4 MB, exactly one 4 MB segment.
  The inode's single-indirect block holds the addresses of those
  segment index blocks: two levels of index for any minute.
